From: Prospero Win contributors <prospero-win@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] server: observe mutex dumps without transferring ownership

Depends on 0810 and applies after the shared-client series. Diagnostic
printing must not set SLOW, adopt a client owner or queue publication.
Print count and opaque owner token from a single atomic snapshot while
published; retain legacy output for SLOW, inactive and retired objects.
The server lock protects metadata. This is observational output, not a
synchronized query or evidence of a console performance improvement.

diff --git a/server/mutex.c b/server/mutex.c
--- a/server/mutex.c
+++ b/server/mutex.c
@@ -285,8 +285,23 @@
 static void mutex_sync_dump( struct object *obj, int verbose )
 {
     struct mutex_sync *mutex = (struct mutex_sync *)obj;
+    (void)verbose;
     assert( obj->ops == &mutex_sync_ops );
-    ps5_mutex_enter_slow( mutex );
+#ifdef WINE_INPROCESS_SERVER
+    if (mutex->fast)
+    {
+        /* The server lock protects the cell pointer and legacy fields.
+         * Clients may change a published word: print one atomic snapshot,
+         * without adopting ownership or changing its mode for diagnostics. */
+        uint64_t word = pw_mutex_word_load( &mutex->fast->word );
+        if (!(word & PW_MUTEX_WORD_SLOW))
+        {
+            fprintf( stderr, "Mutex count=%u owner_token=%u (shared snapshot)\n",
+                     pw_mutex_word_count( word ), pw_mutex_word_owner( word ) );
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     fprintf( stderr, "Mutex count=%u owner=%p\n", mutex->count, mutex->owner );
 }
 
